Z||000005||Standard||03-13-2001||11:40 PM||||If you don't love her and there's nothing you can do to fix the relationship, don't stay together thinking it's gonna be better for your kid.  You'll just end up fighting all the time and putting him through alot more than you should.  I'm not saying to leave him out of your life, just don't put him in the middle of a bad relationship.  My parents are getting divorced after about 20 years of marriage.  It was hard for me when I learned they were thinking about it a year ago, but I've come to terms with it and I know that it's the best thing for everybody.  It's a bit stressful when your parents are fighting all the time.. <P>just my views from my almost 20 years of experience on this place...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||03-13-2001||11:46 PM||||Were going to give it a week or so and see if we can work things out and NOT argue....When the week is up we shall see... I know for now  Luke (our son) would be better off with his mom. ANd maybe in a few years I can have him..Maybe. Im just so wacked out over it. I know its not good for him to be around us fighting, and I want to work everyhitng out so bad, but it may be for the wrong reasons. If it doesnt work out maybe I can find a Fiero girl   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> who knows door locks hehe.......Wish me luck and if your religiuos please say a prair (sp?) been along day.. for me......<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||03-14-2001||03:24 PM||||It's tough to give advice without knowing the situation.  All we know is you are fighting and thinking of leaving.  Generic advice isn't going to help you like "oh, just give it time..."  You want real advice, give us real problems.<P>I'm not being mean, but...don't come to this board and say "My Fiero's broke and I might sell it."  Unless you tell us what's not right, what can we really tell you?  (Oh, it'll work by next week).||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||03-14-2001||06:02 PM||||Married 19 years, been a rough road.  But I've learned a few things that could help...<P>My vote is do not end it!  Period.<BR>But you gotta be willing to think only of what <I>you're</I> doing wrong, and what <I>her</I> needs are.  <I>Forget</I> what she's doing wrong and what your needs are... that will heal in its time, and she'll take care of you once you take care of her.  You ask why should you have to take care of her first?  That's the way it works, that's how they're made.  But that strategy also gets the cart back behind the horse. Put her back on the pedestal like she was when you met.  When she sees you're going to do what it takes, then she will too.  So, first, find out what she says your problems are, and what she needs from you, then take care of it <I>without any expectations in return</I>.  Second, start communicating by repeating back what she says, making sure she means what you think she means.  It works, and although that's not the only communication rule you need to know, it's a start. <BR>Sorry if it sounds like I'm preaching, but you asked.  My marriage isn't perfect, but it's better and it's working.  It's a daily job.  And yes I have considered the effect on the kids and firmly believe I've done the right thing (they say so too).  I'm very happy I followed the above advice, but it's very humbling at first.  Swallow your pride, my man, you'll be glad you did.  <P>||||reg||6
